#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# is_atom

#% text
# `is_atom(x)` gives `true` when `x` is not a compound term: a number, a string or a symbol.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# A complex number is stored as `complex(re, im)`, a compound term, but counts as an atom.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
is_atom(3)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
is_atom("abc")
#% output
#= true

#% cell
is_atom(f(x))
#% output
#= false

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Complex numbers and fractions are atoms:

#% cell
[is_atom(1 + im), is_atom(2/3)]
#% output
#= [true, true]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `is_symbol`, `head`, `leaf_count`, `depth`
